I"�<p>Workplace stress statistics help employers understand a problem, but only when the population, date and method stay attached to the number. A US worker survey, a global mental-health estimate and a historical healthcare-cost model answer different questions.</p>

<p>This guide presents figures traceable to named sources, then explains how institutional learning teams can use them without overstating their meaning. Sources were reviewed on 4 October 2026; each figure retains its own reference period.</p>

